From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: MediaError exposed without VIDEO

The Amiga port builds without ENABLE_VIDEO, and MediaError was
Conditional=VIDEO, so window.MediaError did not exist. Pages that test
"instanceof MediaError" or read MediaError.MEDIA_ERR_* (reddit.com's
scripts do) stopped with "ReferenceError: Can't find variable:
MediaError". The interface (four constants, code and message) is now
built on the Amiga port as well. Nothing creates one, since there are
no media elements; VIDEO stays off.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/html/MediaError.h b/Source/WebCore/html/MediaError.h
index 29b1d63..fb1ac01 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/html/MediaError.h
+++ b/Source/WebCore/html/MediaError.h
@@ -25,7 +25,9 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
-#if ENABLE(VIDEO)
+// Built without VIDEO on the Amiga port as well: the interface is exposed
+// so that pages that test "instanceof MediaError" or read its constants run.
+#if ENABLE(VIDEO) || PLATFORM(AMIGA)
 
 #include <wtf/RefCounted.h>
 #include <wtf/text/WTFString.h>
@@ -64,4 +66,4 @@ private:
 
 } // namespace WebCore
 
-#endif // ENABLE(VIDEO)
+#endif // ENABLE(VIDEO) || PLATFORM(AMIGA)
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/html/MediaError.idl b/Source/WebCore/html/MediaError.idl
index f3d20ab..31d89c2 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/html/MediaError.idl
+++ b/Source/WebCore/html/MediaError.idl
@@ -24,7 +24,6 @@
  */
 
 [
-    Conditional=VIDEO,
     Exposed=Window
 ] interface MediaError {
       const unsigned short MEDIA_ERR_ABORTED = 1;
-- 
